    summary: "AI factories run your repeatable revenue work, measure every outcome and answer to you. Rob Giglio Chief Customer Officer, Canva “We're looking for every place where AI can allow sellers and customer success reps to be more engaged with customers.” Agents@Work → Allen Roh Senior Marketing Manager, Autodesk “The key for us was how we can modularize industry knowledge and the best playbooks, and apply it.” Agents@Work → Remi Pinteau Director of Performance Marketing, Lightspeed Commerce “It's really about saving time, doing things faster, and automating a lot of the most repetitive tasks.” Agents@Work → B Benjamin Cox VP of AI Strategy & Operations, Rakuten Advertising “If the business does the same task a million times, that's where agents can augment, queue, or automate work to create scale.” Agents@Work → Kieran Snaith SVP of Revenue Operations, Qualified “Here's our processes, here's how to think about your job, here are your goals, and immediately that agent is operating on that framework.” Case study → Ryk Neethling CTO, Send Payments “The impacts across our business is not just a little bit of change. It's transformational. We've moved from AI as a potential to an AI-first mindset.” Case study → E Edan Shelley Head of Acquisition and Sales Enablement, Zembl “I'd never go back to manually researching a business. The thought of doing that manually now, it's just not a process we wanna go back to.” “Here's our processes … here are your goals, and imm",
