    logo: "/logos/hadrianio.png",
    stage: "Seed",
    round: null,
    summary: "Hadrian's AI agents map everything you expose, attack it like real adversaries and pentest it continuously. Proof, not noise. Hadrian's agents keep discovering your attack surface, prove which threats are real, and show your team what to fix first. Atlas maps outward from the organization the way an attacker would: subsidiaries and acquisitions, the domains each one registered, then every subdomain, IP, certificate and cloud host under them. Discovery is continuous and responds to change as it happens, so the map is always current. Atlas keeps a live inventory of everything you expose to the internet, so the assets a new zero-day affects are already known. Agents start testing them right away and come back with verified risks, not a list of maybes. Every asset Atlas finds is enriched with context, so even a sprawling attack surface of cloud resources, SaaS apps and shifting IPs makes sense at a glance. Every verified risk arrives prioritized, with its full context and the steps to fix it, so time to remediate drops. Atlas finds what you expose and tests it around the clock. Nova pentests the apps that matter, whenever you need it. Assets, verified risks, owners and alert rules live in one place, and there is nothing to install. Hadrian is at the frontier of agentic AI-driven offensive security with recognition from Gartner®, GigaOm, and Frost & Sullivan. \"For us, Hadrian is a game changer because in one platform, in a few seconds, we could see everything in a live mode.\" Give",
