    logo: "/logos/nium.png",
    stage: "",
    round: null,
    summary: "Nium is global payments infrastructure for real-time cross-border payouts to 190+ countries, card issuance, stablecoin-backed cards, and FX through one API. Pay creators, partners, and vendors, anywhere in the world, on time and in local currency. Receive international payments, pay teams or vendors overseas, and hold or exchange multiple currencies. Where value flows, value grows. Connect currencies, payment rails, onchain networks, and programmable money with one platform. Unlock instant money movement with certainty at every step. Institutional-grade infrastructure — ready for what's next. Financial institutions, global enterprises, and platforms use Nium to enter new markets and scale — without rebuilding their payment stack. Every industry is unique. The need to move money with certainty, globally, and without friction is not. Banks Transform your cross-border payments experience with more real-time payout corridors and local multi-currency accounts. No need to rebuild your infrastructure. Fintechs Move fiat, stablecoins, or both across 190+ countries through one integration, with the payment rails you need to launch new products and scale. Payroll Payday is every day. Pay employees and contractors worldwide, reliably, on time, and in local currency with a single partner who knows how to execute payroll at scale. Spend management Create, operate, and grow your global spend management programs with a robust card issuance stack that includes intelligent FX and flexible con",
    person: null,
    funder: "",
    source: "Company site",
    sourceUrl: "https://www.nium.com/",
    files: [{"title": "About", "text": "Nium is the infrastructure powering the future of money movement — where value flows instantly, globally, and with certainty across any network or chain. Our culture is defined by the global nature of our team. That diversity lets us see the world through a different lens — and build the infrastructure that solves finance's toughest global challenges. 25 COUNTRIES 700 + Employees 47 Nationalities Meet our leadership team. Prajit Nanu Founder and CEO Networks wanted stablecoins operational, not theoretical. Prajit Nanu is the co-founder and CEO of Nium. He launched the company after firsthand experience with the friction of sending money across borders. Since then, he built Nium into an institutional-grade platform for cross-border money movement – with hundreds of category leaders in banking, travel, payroll, tech and AI relying on Nium to collect, convert, send, and spend funds globally. Beyond the CEO role, Prajit leads Nium's product strategy with a focus on embedding compliance and regulatory rigor as a competitive advantage."}],

