    logo: "/logos/bench.png",
    stage: "",
    round: null,
    summary: "Bench pairs you with a dedicated bookkeeper and simple software, so your books get done for you. Trusted by 35,000+ U.S. businesses. See how Bench works. A dedicated bookkeeper does your books. Simple software keeps your financials at your fingertips. Trusted by 35,000+ business owners. We support every industry, from the hair salon on Main Street to the growing digital marketing agency, legal firm, and local coffee shop. 70 industries and counting. Bench supports businesses of all shapes and sizes. Here's how we help a few: Best for businesses that already have a system they like and just need an expert working in it. We'll catch up prior years too, quickly and affordably. Talk to a bookkeeping advisor for a flat quote based on how far behind you are. *Rate based on a 12-month commitment. Must be purchased at least 3 months prior to tax filing deadline; otherwise, discounted annual pricing applies. Clients are welcome to BYOB (Bring Your Own Bookkeeping). Books are subject to review—if additional cleanup or preparation is needed to file, discounted bookkeeping services will be offered. *Monthly pricing requires a 12-month commitment and must be purchased at least 3 months prior to your tax filing deadline (otherwise discounted annual pricing applies). Catch-up bookkeeping is billed at a discounted bundle rate when paired with an annual bookkeeping/tax package. Filing timelines depend on prompt submission of historical financial records. *For customers who have filed with Ben",
    person: null,
    funder: "",
    source: "Company site",
    sourceUrl: "https://www.bench.co/",
    files: [{"title": "About", "text": "Bench is an online bookkeeping service for U.S.-based businesses, small and growing — operating today as an Employer.com company. We started Bench to take bookkeeping off business owners' plates for good — so you can spend your time running your business, not reconciling it. Bench is fully operational, staffed by its in-house team, with Employer.com continuing to invest in the bookkeeping business. Their bookkeeping services have helped me keep my numbers straight and they are always available to answer questions. The new owners have made a noticeable difference in processes.\" Bench uses read-only access to your financial accounts — your transactions can be imported for bookkeeping, but no one can move your money. Every bookkeeper passes background checks, and you can export your completed work anytime, even after your subscription ends."}],

