    id: "figures",
    name: "Figures",
    website: "https://figures.hr/",
    logo: "/logos/figures.png",
    stage: "",
    round: null,
    summary: "Salary benchmarking, pay equity analysis, and EU Pay Transparency Directive compliance in one platform. Trusted by 500+ companies across Europe. Get ready for the EU Pay Transparency Directive with powerful and intuitive analytics tools. Maintain up-to-date, consistent salary bands to unify and guide all your compensation decisions. Structure your compensation reviews with clear steps and live tracking of both progress and budget. Spot company-wide and individual pay gaps, and follow tailored recommendations to explain or close them. Figures connects with 30+ HRIS and review systems, enhancing them with external data, manager-friendly tools, and compliance-ready modules. Sharpen your skills Customer success story How HolidayPirates Built Transparent, Data-Backed Salary Bands with Figures Customer success story How Welcome to the Jungle developed their salary bands with Figures Customer success story How Swan uses the Salary Review module to save time and improve efficiency Simplify your compensation management today Intuitive, collaborative tools to structure your compensation decisions.",
    person: null,
    funder: "",
    source: "Company site",
    sourceUrl: "https://figures.hr/",
    files: [{"title": "About", "text": "After years of spreadsheet chaos and unreliable data, we built Figures to bring clarity, collaboration, and fairness to compensation management. With pay transparency laws reshaping the landscape, the pressure to justify salaries is growing. Figures gives HR and managers the tools to put people first—aligning pay with business goals while staying ahead of compliance. You don't have to be serious to do serious work. We value fun in our day to day and we try not to be boring in our communication. We don't want to hire \"executants\" - we're looking for people that will challenge existing processes, strategies, tools, and \"own\" their scope. In order to be efficient as a company and for everyone to have a maximum impact we want everyone to be autonomous and free to act as possible."}],

